│ {'review_title': 'Chemotherapy for advanced, recurrent or metastatic endometrial carcinoma', 'review_background':    │
│ 'Although endometrial adenocarcinoma is a common gynaecological cancer, a comparatively small proportion of patients │
│ present with, or develop, recurrent or advanced disease. However, for those women whose disease does progress or     │
│ recur the prognosis is poor and the best treatment is yet to be identified. Co‐morbidity, including obesity and      │
